    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and high-leverage plate appearances against favorable opposing arms. **Corbin Carroll** (79.45) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) headline our starters; **Corbin Carroll** overcomes a slight L/L platoon disadvantage against Abbott with an elite order slot and projected speed contributions, while **Tyler Soderstrom** exploits a soft matchup against Sugano to maximize his output. **Jose Caballero** (75.83) also presents a high-floor play, benefiting from a 13% boost due to a dynamic platoon edge that effectively mitigates his neutral park factors. These three serve as our primary offensive engine, with **Josh Naylor** (72.85) rounding out our elite tier as he prepares to capitalize on Poulin\u2019s high expected ERA.\n\n**Max Muncy** (57.67) represents the most intriguing decision on the roster, narrowly securing a start over our available bench options. While his raw projection against Sugano was modest, the lack of depth due to the IL statuses of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** forces our hand; he remains the most efficient choice despite his #7 spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Dalton Rushing** (44.94) and **Alex Freeland** (48.58) anchor the bottom of our efficiency rankings. Both are hampered by #8 and #9 order slots, respectively, and a challenging matchup against Hudson; however, they remain in the lineup to protect against the high risk of empty starts from the bench, such as **Seiya Suzuki**, who is not in today's lineup.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk factors for **Austin Riley** (53.34) closely. His score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Peralta\u2014a pitcher who ranks as one of the more formidable arms on today's slate\u2014and a slight negative park factor. While we rely on **Austin Riley** for power, his current efficiency score reflects the reality that he is facing a tough pitcher in a less-than-ideal environment. We remain cautious regarding **James Wood** (65.20) as well; while his xwOBA is elite, the presence of a pitcher with a 4.00 xERA and effective base-stealing prevention tactics tempers our expectations for his total contribution to our SB-starved campaign. Owners should note that our depth, including players like **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Henry Bolte**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana**, remains on standby should any late-inning defensive replacements or weather-related delays shift the projected usage.",
